{"id":"paul","name":"Paul","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:paul"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Paul","text":"=Saul (q.v.) was born about the same time as our Lord. His circumcision-name was Saul, and probably the name Paul was also given to him in infancy “for use in the Gentile world,” as “Saul” would be his Hebrew home-name. He was a native of Tarsus, the capital of Cilicia, a Roman province in the south-east of Asia Minor. That city stood on the banks of the river Cydnus, which was navigable thus far; hence it became a centre of extensive commercial traffic with many countries along the shores of the Mediterranean, as well as with the countries of central Asia Minor. It thus became a city distinguished for the wealth of its inhabitants. Tarsus was also the seat of a famous university, higher in reputation even than the universities of Athens and Alexandria, the only others that then existed. Here Saul was born, and here he spent his youth, doubtless enjoying the best education his native …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","xlit":"Paûlos","gloss":", meaning the same)","kjv":"Paul, Paulus","count":123,"share":0.2},{"strong":"G5037","lemma":"τέ","xlit":"té","gloss":"both or also )","kjv":"also, and, both, even","count":68,"share":0.11},{"strong":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","xlit":"Ioudaîos","gloss":"Judæan","kjv":"Jew, of Judæa","count":59,"share":0.1},{"strong":"G435","lemma":"ἀνήρ","xlit":"anḗr","gloss":"a man","kjv":"fellow, husband, man, sir","count":48,"share":0.08},{"strong":"G2596","lemma":"κατά","xlit":"katá","gloss":"down , in varied relations with which it is joined)","kjv":"about, according as, after, against","count":55,"share":0.09},{"strong":"G2250","lemma":"ἡμέρα","xlit":"hēméra","gloss":"the time space between dawn and dark, or the whole 24 ho","kjv":"age, + alway, day ), + for ever","count":54,"share":0.09}],"verses":["Acts.13.7","Acts.13.9","Acts.13.13","Acts.13.16","Acts.13.50","Acts.14.